WEBVTT

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:02.400
Yes! Gotcha!

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:04.720
Good luck, me!

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:07.740
The veterans took both games!

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.740
I'd like to withdraw from the second match.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:12.480
He's toying with you!

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:14.220
Arata.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.980
What did you tell him, Chihaya?

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:42.530
Just something I thought of 
when I was watching him.

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:43.300
Hey!

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:47.310
The entire Shiranami Society was 
all gung-ho about beating Arata!

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.960
Do you want him to win now?

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:54.070
<b>Master and Queen Challenger Playoffs 
Sponsored by the National Karuta Association</b>

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:53.420
That's not it.

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:57.820
Only the one who gives their 
all to win can reach the top.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:59.740
Isn't that what the finals are about?

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:08.120
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:09.950
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:17.030
Verse 13

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:17.030
Yet it is
 I who
 withers
 and wilts

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:14.930
I can't believe what Harada-san did.

00:02:14.930 --> 00:02:17.610
I've never seen anyone 
withdraw during the finals.

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:20.610
He's honestly unbelievable.

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:24.490
But depending on how you look at it, 
this could be the ultimate strategy.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:28.660
It doesn't change the fact that he 
needs one more victory to win it all.

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:30.910
Rather than play consecutive 
games against a young opponent,

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:35.060
he's taking a loss for a chance to recover 
his strength for the third match.

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:37.070
If the next reader is one 
he works well with,

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:38.500
that makes his choice even better.

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:42.110
Hey, you two! Don't defend what he's doing!

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:44.950
He's just stringing everyone 
along out of pure ego!

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:46.140
O-Of course...

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:51.050
I hope Igarashi-san, the next 
reader, wasn't offended...

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:51.060
<b>Tweet Tweet</b>

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:55.070
<b>About to start reading for the second match
 in the challenger finals. The joy of being 
able to read just for Haruka-chan and
Megumu-chan in the Queen challenger
 finals... Priceless!</b>

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:57.570
About to start reading
 for the second match
 in the challenger finals.
 The joy of being 
able to read just for
 Haruka-chan and
Megumu-chan in
 the Queen challenger
 finals... Priceless!

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:58.480
<i>It's just us two in the second match.</i>

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.360
What the heck? What the heck?!

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:04.740
I was wearing it like this the whole time?!

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:06.290
<b>She figured it out</b>

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:06.280
You're kidding!

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:19.120
H-Here you go, queen!

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:23.670
A-Aki...

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:25.600
I'm not a queen yet.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.940
Let me borrow your headbands!

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:56.450
She tied them together!

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:03.110
We're both so blessed, aren't we?

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:06.290
What's the deal with this year's finals?

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:08.690
<i>This is a first in all kinds of ways...</i>

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:12.510
None of the players are 
concerned about how they look.

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:15.990
<i>Lucky... They're so lucky...</i>

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:19.270
You too, Taichi.

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:23.110
If you had won, you'd be playing here, too.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:28.350
Wouldn't that be amazing? I wish 
we could have played here.

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:31.520
Even if you don't care 
about being the Master...

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:39.550
It's time to begin.

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:48.390
<i>Naniwa Bay, now the flower 
blooms, but for winter</i>

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:58.530
<i>Here comes spring, now the flower blooms</i>

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:05.080
<i>The emotions experienced after 
a long-awaited reunion</i>

00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:01.830
<i>She's fast.</i>

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:04.040
<i>Even faster than last year.</i>

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:07.410
<i>This is her second challenger final,</i>

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:11.070
<i>and she only lost to Inokuma-san 
by two cards in the first match.</i>

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:14.700
<i>You don't want to take her 
too lightly, Haruka-san.</i>

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:18.990
<i>Yu-chan came to watch</i>

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:22.310
<i>the West Japan qualifiers, even 
though she has exams to study for.</i>

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:26.070
<i>She even came all the way 
out here to cheer me on.</i>

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:30.650
<i>You don't need to worry 
about that, Megumu-tan!</i>

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:34.210
<i>If I lose after putting these 
things on, I'll be humiliated.</i>

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:36.090
<i>Yes! That's it!</i>

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:39.740
<i>She's lunging more slowly.</i>

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:42.850
<i>Did her fear of faulting dull her reflexes?</i>

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:45.540
<i>This isn't like you, Haruka-san.</i>

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:49.180
<i>You'll lose if you get rid 
of your best weapon.</i>

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:52.560
If you can hear better, 
you can take them, too!

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:57.540
<i>Sakurazawa-san...</i>

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:01.220
<i>That was such an arrogant 
thing to say to you.</i>

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:04.260
<i>Rain takes longer to dry...</i>

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:05.270
<i>That was fast!</i>

00:06:05.270 --> 00:06:08.460
<i>"Rain" is a one-syllable card. 
That's Inokuma-san for you.</i>

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:12.300
<i>She heard the half-tone? No...</i>

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:18.770
<i>for I could not recognize you,
 like the moon hidden 
behind the clouds</i>

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:18.770
<i>leaving a hovering 
mist above the 
trees and grass</i>

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:15.400
<i>She stalled because "Long" 
is still in play.</i>

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:18.430
<i>But she's been reacting to 
those sounds all this time...</i>

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.960
<i>Is the girl who said she takes 
cards because she hears well</i>

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:25.510
<i>suddenly conscious of the sound that 
comes before the unique syllable?</i>

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:29.390
<i>I don't want to commit another 
fault by acting on a gut feeling.</i>

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:32.250
<i>I've lost that way too many times.</i>

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:35.750
<i>And when I lost, I thought...</i>

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:39.540
<i>I can be even better.</i>

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:44.010
<i>If people never lose, they never change.</i>

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:45.760
<i>They never grow stronger.</i>

00:06:47.030 --> 00:06:48.840
<i>By losing, you can change!</i>

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:50.630
<i>You can become stronger!</i>

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:56.380
<i>She always had naturally good game sense,</i>

00:06:56.380 --> 00:06:58.840
<i>and now she's even greedier for sound...</i>

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:03.480
<i>and more careful.</i>

00:07:07.270 --> 00:07:09.120
Thank you very much.

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:16.130
With two wins in a row, the challenger to 
the Queen will be Inokuma Haruka, grade 6!

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:21.600
W-Wow, Inokuma-san was really good.

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:24.300
How did that compare to 
when you played her?

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:26.950
Chi...

00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:28.360
Chihaya?

00:07:30.230 --> 00:07:31.400
Dr. Harada...

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:33.460
The second match is over.

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:37.160
Inokuma-san won, and the third 
match is starting soon.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:41.100
I'm starving...

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:42.960
Do you need to eat something?

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:44.720
I have some rice balls and chocolate...

00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:46.100
No, that's all right.

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:49.300
I don't know how much I'll have.

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:50.100
Huh?

00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:54.480
I don't know how many calories 
I'll have when I celebrate later.

00:07:55.790 --> 00:07:59.170
Arata-kun, where'd you go? Arata-kun...

00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:01.500
He just said he was going 
for a little walk.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:02.990
Did he get lost?

00:08:02.990 --> 00:08:04.350
Arata!

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:05.490
Oh, here he comes.

00:08:21.710 --> 00:08:23.930
Now Wataya-kun's the one who's late.

00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:26.260
They both have one win and one loss.

00:08:27.350 --> 00:08:29.240
<i>They may both have one win and one loss,</i>

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:31.720
<i>but Wataya-kun's win came 
from being yielded to.</i>

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:35.730
<i>Harada-san's tactics are truly brutal.</i>

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:39.860
<i>Come on, Chihaya! Where'd you go?</i>

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:42.930
<i>One more win.</i>

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:45.320
<i>Who's going to snatch it?</i>

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:17.570
Third Match Reader 
Makino Midori, Grade 6

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:22.070
<i>I like the way Makino-san's 
been reading lately.</i>

00:09:22.630 --> 00:09:25.350
<i>The weird idiosyncrasies she had 
when she was young are gone.</i>

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:26.990
<i>The length of her reverberation</i>

00:09:26.990 --> 00:09:29.890
<i>and her speed leading up to unique 
syllables have stabilized.</i>

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:32.710
<i>And above all...</i>

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:39.770
<i>Naniwa Bay, now the flower 
blooms, but for winter</i>

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:48.470
<i>Here comes spring, now the flower blooms</i>

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:49.900
<i>Her nasal tone is beautiful.</i>

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:58.100
<i>Here comes spring, now the flower blooms</i>

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:05.420
<i>When winds send waves crashing 
against the rocks in vain,</i>

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:01.370
Yes!

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:02.080
<i>Yes!</i>

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:03.290
<i>Yes, Dr. Harada!</i>

00:10:31.630 --> 00:10:35.190
<i>...is like flowing water.</i>

00:10:35.490 --> 00:10:37.340
Hup...

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:43.380
<i>That's... his grandpa's kimono...</i>

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:51.340
<i>And the way the metal fittings on the heel 
of his sandal brush the floor as he walks...</i>

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:56.160
Arata.

00:10:57.030 --> 00:11:01.880
No matter how far you go, Dr. Harada 
is still a mentor to all of us.

00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:06.140
You can't beat him as just Arata.

00:11:29.060 --> 00:11:31.770
Want another one?

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:41.760
<b>Kyoiku no Mori Park</b>

00:11:33.820 --> 00:11:36.890
<i>Kyoiku no Mori Park in Bunkyo Ward</i>

00:11:36.890 --> 00:11:38.960
<i>is a place not far from the karuta hall</i>

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:41.350
<i>where locals can relax among 
the water and greenery.</i>

00:11:42.170 --> 00:11:44.100
<i>Snowmaru dorayaki</i>

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:47.630
<i>began with a mascot from the Kinki 
region that gained a following</i>

00:11:47.630 --> 00:11:50.010
<i>and is now a huge hit in dorayaki form.</i>

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:54.230
<i>I thought it was about as 
obscure as Daddy Bear,</i>

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:56.600
<i>but it's clearly starting 
to leave him in the dust.</i>

00:11:56.600 --> 00:11:58.050
<i>And it's so good,</i>

00:11:58.050 --> 00:12:00.610
<i>with the tapioca in its red bean 
paste that looks like snow!</i>

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:09.380
Are you sure you should be out here 
eating dorayaki, Class A girl?

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:10.580
<b>Shock</b>

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:15.200
<i>Why am I not here as a participant?!</i>

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:17.120
<i>They're so lucky...</i>

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:19.840
<i>Inokuma-san and Megumu-chan are so lucky!</i>

00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:26.060
I came here to Kyoto for my class trip.

00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:27.690
I'll never have a second chance.

00:12:28.630 --> 00:12:29.870
It's fine.

00:12:30.670 --> 00:12:32.660
I'll be in the Queen tournament next year.

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:37.760
<i>I want to ask him...</i>

00:12:39.510 --> 00:12:43.900
U-Um, why do you always hand out pastries?

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:44.970
<i>...so many things.</i>

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:47.610
Japanese pastries are full of vitamins.

00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:50.110
<i>Vitamins? That's unexpected!</i>

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:54.120
Wh-Why do you always speak so quietly?

00:12:57.640 --> 00:13:00.770
Is that all you want to ask me?

00:13:03.710 --> 00:13:05.380
Suo-san! Do you—

00:13:06.750 --> 00:13:08.590
I'm so sorry!

00:13:08.590 --> 00:13:09.960
A-A-A-Are you okay?!

00:13:09.960 --> 00:13:11.320
I'm sorry!

00:13:11.320 --> 00:13:12.850
You should've ducked, man!

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:14.090
Don't just tell him to duck!

00:13:17.990 --> 00:13:19.180
Thanks.

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:24.440
<i>What I want to ask Suo-san...</i>

00:13:27.020 --> 00:13:29.610
<i>is about his extraordinary game sense.</i>

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:34.550
Suo-san...

00:13:35.270 --> 00:13:38.750
Will you play a match with me sometime?

00:13:45.370 --> 00:13:49.060
Isn't there something else?

00:13:51.590 --> 00:13:52.430
I...

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:54.180
I don't have a girlfrie—

00:13:55.380 --> 00:13:57.260
The time! It's already 2:00!

00:13:57.260 --> 00:13:59.160
The third match is starting, Suo-san!

00:13:59.430 --> 00:14:01.850
Hurry, Suo-san! Hurry!

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:04.900
I don't have a girlfrie—

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:06.590
Suo-san, hurry!

00:14:08.340 --> 00:14:10.260
I don't have... a girlfriend.

00:14:10.260 --> 00:14:11.660
The light's green!

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:11.660
<b>Press button to activate at night</b>

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:12.660
I... I don't...

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:15.840
Listen to me! I don't have a girlfriend!

00:14:15.840 --> 00:14:17.650
Neither do I!

00:14:22.680 --> 00:14:24.430
Suo-san, hurry!

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:26.670
<i>My bride...</i>

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:27.780
<i>You're skipping?!</i>

00:14:36.260 --> 00:14:40.220
<i>What is this atmosphere?</i>

00:14:43.740 --> 00:14:45.700
<i>I feel as though...</i>

00:14:44.790 --> 00:14:45.700
Yes!

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:58.960
<i>burning brightly by night, 
yet extinguished by day</i>

00:14:50.250 --> 00:14:53.070
<i>With "I feel as" gone, 
he sent "I feel that."</i>

00:14:53.070 --> 00:14:55.310
<i>That's in line with Dr. Harada's theory.</i>

00:14:56.140 --> 00:14:58.970
<i>Most people would put it 
where "I feel as" was,</i>

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:02.790
<i>Wataya Arata's Preferred Layout</i>

00:14:58.970 --> 00:15:02.390
<i>but with Wataya Arata's preferred layout, 
it'll be in the lower left row...</i>

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:08.520
<i>The center left row?</i>

00:15:08.520 --> 00:15:10.290
I'm moving my cards.

00:15:11.150 --> 00:15:14.070
<i>And he moved "So spring nights" 
to the center right...</i>

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:17.710
<i>What is he thinking?</i>

00:15:19.220 --> 00:15:21.190
<i>Would the mountain cherry blossoms...</i>

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:21.820
<i>Dr. Harada got two in a row!</i>

00:15:21.820 --> 00:15:22.220
<i>All right!</i>

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:27.940
<i>But unlike in the first match, Wataya 
Arata's not going for any cards.</i>

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:35.910
<i>be as dear now, those 
were the good old days</i>

00:15:30.270 --> 00:15:33.320
<i>Dr. Harada took "Would the" 
and sent "Would this."</i>

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:35.670
<i>That card often comes down 
to a contest of speed.</i>

00:15:35.670 --> 00:15:38.560
<i>Surely Wataya-kun will put 
it in his preferred spot...</i>

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:40.870
<b>Would this</b>

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:41.210
<i>The center right?!</i>

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:43.130
<b>So spring nights</b>

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:44.440
<i>And he moved "So spring nights" 
back to where it was before!</i>

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:49.380
<i>What is he thinking?</i>

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:55.430
<b>Sheesh</b>

00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:56.890
<i>No matter how much the cards move, 
I have to check them over carefully.</i>

00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:58.980
<i>Make a note of every last point...</i>

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:04.440
<i>While it brings</i>

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:04.440
<i>While it may</i>

00:16:00.410 --> 00:16:03.860
<i>Glasses has "While it brings" and 
"While it may" side by side.</i>

00:16:04.670 --> 00:16:07.250
<i>Is he thinking of aiming 
for my "While it pains"</i>

00:16:07.250 --> 00:16:09.660
<i>and being able to take them on the return?</i>

00:16:10.290 --> 00:16:11.570
<i>I won't let him!</i>

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:13.150
<i>While some dodge...</i>

00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:16.380
<i>He easily went for "While some" before 
even reaching for "While it pains"?</i>

00:16:17.170 --> 00:16:20.360
<i>Dr. Harada had "While it brings" and "While 
it may" marked, but he was too slow.</i>

00:16:22.720 --> 00:16:25.470
<i>I have no idea what he's thinking.</i>

00:16:25.470 --> 00:16:29.450
<i>What is this awful, awful style of karuta?</i>

00:16:31.350 --> 00:16:33.540
<i>I feel that my love...</i>

00:16:36.230 --> 00:16:39.220
<i>"I feel as" ended up back 
in its original position.</i>

00:16:39.810 --> 00:16:44.110
<i>Dr. Harada went so far as to memorize 
Wataya-kun's preferred layout.</i>

00:16:44.110 --> 00:16:46.400
<i>It hurts when his guesses are off.</i>

00:16:46.930 --> 00:16:51.360
<i>How can a high school kid who's only 
17 come up with such tactics?</i>

00:16:52.600 --> 00:16:54.450
Oh, thanks.

00:16:56.650 --> 00:16:59.480
<i>Wait... was that Taichi?</i>

00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:04.970
<i>Grandpa...</i>

00:17:06.090 --> 00:17:10.270
<i>What would you say if you'd been 
watching me in the first match?</i>

00:17:12.750 --> 00:17:15.370
<i>"You're trying, but you're 
not there just yet."</i>

00:17:15.910 --> 00:17:17.510
<i>"You're still young."</i>

00:17:19.270 --> 00:17:21.390
<i>And what would he say to Dr. Harada?</i>

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:27.530
<i>"You're still young, too."</i>

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:36.820
<i>My own sleeves are like...</i>

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:43.200
<i>What is this?</i>

00:17:44.470 --> 00:17:47.330
<i>Even Harada's playing 
is starting to look...</i>

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:55.080
<i>The one time I played 
against Master Wataya...</i>

00:17:55.620 --> 00:17:58.840
<i>It was an invitational 
tournament, when I was 19.</i>

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:03.070
<i>He was 15 years older than 
me, and already the Master.</i>

00:18:03.070 --> 00:18:05.180
<i>The Alain Delon of the karuta world...</i>

00:18:06.700 --> 00:18:08.110
<i>My role model!</i>

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:15.910
I'm moving my cards.

00:18:18.940 --> 00:18:22.590
<i>He put all the one-syllable 
cards in the lower right!</i>

00:18:22.590 --> 00:18:24.870
<i>He's determined to make him aim there!</i>

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:28.280
<i>That's a trick Master Wataya often used 
against offensive karuta players!</i>

00:18:29.320 --> 00:18:32.200
<i>Master Wataya's play style...</i>

00:18:35.200 --> 00:18:36.290
<i>I'll break through it!</i>

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:40.840
<i>I'll make you regret putting all your 
one-syllable cards in your lower right!</i>

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:43.980
<i>No big deal!</i>

00:18:44.800 --> 00:18:46.400
<i>Next time!</i>

00:18:49.690 --> 00:18:52.590
<i>From the way he handles his 
cards to his expression...</i>

00:18:53.100 --> 00:18:55.470
<i>It's like I'm looking at Master Wataya.</i>

00:18:55.910 --> 00:18:57.960
Envision your own victory.

00:18:58.350 --> 00:19:02.000
<i>All the things Master Wataya was 
always saying to Arata-kun</i>

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:05.540
<i>are coming to life now, in this form...</i>

00:19:07.210 --> 00:19:11.660
<i>The one thing Arata-kun lacked was 
experience on a major stage,</i>

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:15.540
<i>and the image of Master Wataya 
is filling that void.</i>

00:19:15.540 --> 00:19:17.570
<i>So spring ends...</i>

00:19:17.570 --> 00:19:19.160
<i>Dr. Harada double faulted!</i>

00:19:19.160 --> 00:19:23.550
<i>I was tempted by the "So spring nights" 
that he kept moving around!</i>

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:29.190
Damn it!

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:29.180
<b>Double Fault 
The player is sent two cards:
 one for the card taken from them,
 and one for the fault</b>

00:19:36.360 --> 00:19:37.970
<i>Arata has ten cards,</i>

00:19:37.970 --> 00:19:39.920
<i>and Dr. Harada has fifteen.</i>

00:19:39.920 --> 00:19:41.590
<i>The gap is growing.</i>

00:19:42.430 --> 00:19:45.740
<i>Harada looks like he's enjoying this...</i>

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:49.490
<i>Harada...</i>

00:19:51.130 --> 00:19:53.870
<i>Isn't this enough already, Harada?</i>

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:59.390
<i>He's such a promising talent, such a 
treasure for the future of karuta.</i>

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:04.530
<i>Just burn out already, Harada.</i>

00:20:06.130 --> 00:20:07.730
<i>I'm so happy.</i>

00:20:08.940 --> 00:20:10.800
<i>So happy...</i>

00:20:12.050 --> 00:20:16.690
<i>I never thought I'd get to feel like 
a teenager playing karuta again!</i>

00:20:19.020 --> 00:20:20.500
<i>This is fun.</i>

00:20:21.430 --> 00:20:23.610
<i>I have to give all I have.</i>

00:20:24.560 --> 00:20:26.860
<i>And even if I lose after that...</i>

00:20:31.590 --> 00:20:33.190
<i>My knee...</i>

00:20:54.240 --> 00:20:56.460
<i>He's down seven to thirteen.</i>

00:20:56.460 --> 00:20:57.640
<i>Dr. Harada!</i>

00:20:58.070 --> 00:20:59.900
<i>Is his knee hurting again?</i>

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:02.520
<i>Don't push yourself, Harada!</i>

00:21:02.950 --> 00:21:04.350
<i>Now his knee...</i>

00:21:04.820 --> 00:21:08.270
<i>Wataya-kun has a clear advantage now.</i>

00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:14.090
Dr. Harada's great.

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:16.390
He's exciting.

00:21:18.890 --> 00:21:20.000
If I...

00:21:21.720 --> 00:21:24.180
could pick who I face in 
the Master tournament,

00:21:24.180 --> 00:21:26.000
I'd want it to be Dr. Harada.
